<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI World air cargo up 9.7pct in Nov 96.</title>
<headline>ACI World air cargo up 9.7pct in Nov 96.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in the Airports Council International (ACI) six geographical regions in November 1996, with percentage change on November 1995, the Geneva body said.</p>
<p>		     NOVEMBER 1996</p>
<p>			    Tonnes	 Pct change on</p>
<p>					     November 1995</p>
<p> Africa			43,524    up 103.6pct</p>
<p> Asia/Pacific	     942,440    up  11.7</p>
<p> Europe		     935,835    up   7.4</p>
<p> L.America/Carribean    114,786    up  37.5</p>
<p> Middle East		139,852    up  16.9</p>
<p> North America	  2,255,522    up   7.5</p>
<p> Total		    4,431,959    up   9.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017 Freight and mail traffic handled by 473 airports around the world in November 1996, totalled 4,431,959 million tonnes, up 9.7 percent on the same month the previous year,</p>
